## Limitations recorded honestly

- Dark-theme figure re-shots: the reviewer's driver could not force the site's dark theme
  (setting html[data-theme=dark] and localStorage 'theme' produced byte-identical images to the
  light shots; the site's theme initialiser overrides both). Dark-variant verification therefore
  rests on: the .ur.dark.svg source bytes (both repaired labels verified present by direct
  extraction), the build assets being byte-identical to static/ sources (site-build.log), and
  render-inspect section A confirming both variants serve on every carrier. Cycle 1's
  renders-feat023-r1/figure-U5-4-ur-dark.png and figure-U5-8-ur-dark.png remain the visual dark
  evidence for the unrepaired labels; the repaired labels are verified in source and build bytes.
- No system Noto Nastaliq Urdu is installed on this host for SVG-internal figure text (the .ur.svg
  files use system font stacks and embed no font), so figure-internal glyphs render in fallback
  Arabic shaping in the browser screenshots; page body text is unaffected (the self-hosted webfont
  loads - targeted-shots.log). Figure-internal Nastaliq verification on a Nastaliq-capable host
  remains an owner-side check, as in the Unit 3/4 G5 runs (carried advisory).
- pdftoppm is not installed on this host, so the A4 print PDFs were not rasterised for visual
  reading; print evidence is the render-inspect section C measurements (clippedElems 0, all
  figures within 794px) plus the committed PDF artifacts themselves.
